{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016bvxtk6f3Vpn9yJBvcFBnh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '因果诊断在 Walker Walk 仍成立但需加 nuance。标题用 \"Diagnosing Value Overestimation\n2\t  in Temporally-Abstract World Models\"。 C2 措辞从 \"root cause\" 调为 \"primary contributing\n3\t  factor in Walker Walk\"。 Cheetah Run 引入 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 讨论——RSSM\n4\t  prediction error 的环境依赖性调节 dt_embedding 危害程度。 v/e overshoot ratio 从硬规则降为启发式。Discussion\n5\t  增加 \"boundary conditions\" 分析。\n6\t\n7\t  '\n8\timagined_experiments:\n9\t- name: Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\n10\t  plan_id: plan_010\n11\t  description: 2 additional seeds for dt=1 baseline, establishing per-seed v/e calibration\n12\t    curves\n13\t  expected_results:\n14\t    seed1_eval_return_55K: 610\n15\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 890\n16\t    seed1_eval_return_last10_mean: 935\n17\t    seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.255\n18\t    seed1_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.42\n19\t    seed1_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.67\n20\t    seed2_eval_return_55K: 580\n21\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 870\n22\t    seed2_eval_return_last10_mean: 920\n23\t    seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.22\n24\t    seed2_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.38\n25\t    seed2_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.64\n26\t    cross_seed_mean_last10: 935\n27\t    cross_seed_std_last10: 15\n28\t    cross_seed_ve_stable_range: 67-74%\n29\t  result_rationale: 'Walker Walk dt=1 baseline 在 DreamerV3 中是成熟配置，seed 间 variance\n30\t    较小。 Seed 0 asymptote 950.9，预期 seed 1-2 在 920-950 范围内（±3%），v/e 稳态在 67-74%。 这是 median\n31\t    档的正常 baseline variance，不影响因果链判断。 v/e calibration curves 形状一致（单调上升后饱和），但具体数值有 ±0.03\n32\t    偏移， 这会为后续 normalized v/e 计算引入小幅 per-seed 校准差异。\n33\t\n34\t    '\n35\t  tables:\n36\t  - name: Baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\n37\t    columns:\n38\t    - step\n39\t    - seed0_ve\n40\t    - seed1_ve\n41\t    - seed2_ve\n42\t    - mean_ve\n43\t    - std_ve\n44\t    rows:\n45\t    - - 25K\n46\t      - 0.087\n47\t      - 0.095\n48\t      - 0.08\n49\t      - 0.087\n50\t      - 0.006\n51\t    - - 35K\n52\t      - 0.241\n53\t      - 0.255\n54\t      - 0.22\n55\t      - 0.239\n56\t      - 0.014\n57\t    - - 55K\n58\t      - 0.404\n59\t      - 0.42\n60\t      - 0.38\n61\t      - 0.401\n62\t      - 0.016\n63\t    - - 105K\n64\t      - 0.656\n65\t      - 0.67\n66\t      - 0.64\n67\t      - 0.655\n68\t      - 0.012\n69\t  figures_description:\n70\t  - 3-seed baseline learning curves (eval return vs step), shaded std band. All converge\n71\t    to ~920-950 by 200K.\n72\t  - 3-seed v/e ratio curves overlaid. Near-identical shape, stable from 135K+.\n73\t  analysis: 'Baseline 的 3-seed 一致性高（CV<2%），为 normalized v/e 的 per-seed 计算提供可靠参考。 v/e\n74\t    stable range 67-74% 跨 seed，比单 seed 的 69-72% 稍宽，但仍是紧致分布。 这意味着 >1.5x normalized\n75\t    v/e 阈值在 3-seed 下仍有足够 margin。\n76\t\n77\t    '\n78\t- name: Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\n79\t  plan_id: plan_011\n80\t  description: 'Replicate delusional critic collapse: subsample ON + trained dt_emb\n81\t    + H=8'\n82\t  expected_results:\n83\t    seed1_eval_return_25K: 155\n84\t    seed1_eval_return_35K: 138\n85\t    seed1_eval_return_45K: 125\n86\t    seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.45\n87\t    seed1_value_eval_ratio_45K: 0.72\n88\t    seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.76\n89\t    seed1_normalized_ve_45K: 2.17\n90\t    seed1_verdict: COLLAPSE_CONFIRMED\n91\t    seed2_eval_return_25K: 180\n92\t    seed2_eval_return_35K: 170\n93\t    seed2_eval_return_45K: 162\n94\t    seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.35\n95\t    seed2_value_eval_ratio_45K: 0.55\n96\t    seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.59\n97\t    seed2_normalized_ve_45K: 1.66\n98\t    seed2_verdict: DEGRADATION_NO_FULL_COLLAPSE\n99\t    collapse_replication_count: 2\n100\t    cross_seed_mean_eval_45K: 143\n101\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：008d collapse 在 2/3 seeds 复现，1 seed 仅 degradation\n102\t    不 collapse。 Seed 0 已确认 collapse（eval 167→146→141, normalized v/e 1.78x→2.09x）。\n103\t    Seed 1 预期复现类似 pattern：v/e 加速 diverge，eval 持续下降，构成 collapse。 Seed 2 是 median 档的关键区分点——trained\n104\t    dt_emb 仍导致 elevated normalized v/e（>1.5x）， 但 eval 仅从 180 缓降到 162 而非 crash，v/e\n105\t    加速率较低。 可能原因：seed 2 的 RSSM 恰好在 dt=2 transition 上学到了稍好的 representation， 使 value\n106\t    overestimation 速度放慢但不消除。这给了足够 signal 说 trained dt_emb 有害， 但 variance 阻止了 \"100%\n107\t    collapse\" 的强结论，需用 \"primary contributing factor\" 措辞。\n108\t\n109\t    '\n110\t  tables:\n111\t  - name: 008d collapse replication (3 seeds)\n112\t    columns:\n113\t    - step\n114\t    - seed0_eval\n115\t    - seed1_eval\n116\t    - seed2_eval\n117\t    - seed0_nve\n118\t    - seed1_nve\n119\t    - seed2_nve\n120\t    rows:\n121\t    - - 25K\n122\t      - 167\n123\t      - 155\n124\t      - 180\n125\t      - 1.78\n126\t      - 1.73\n127\t      - 1.52\n128\t    - - 35K\n129\t      - 146\n130\t      - 138\n131\t      - 170\n132\t      - 1.71\n133\t      - 1.76\n134\t      - 1.59\n135\t    - - 45K\n136\t      - 141\n137\t      - 125\n138\t      - 162\n139\t      - 2.09\n140\t      - 2.17\n141\t      - 1.66\n142\t  figures_description:\n143\t  - 3-seed 008d learning curves. Seed 0,1 show clear collapse; seed 2 shows degradation\n144\t    with slower decline.\n145\t  - 3-seed normalized v/e trajectories. All >1.5x, but seed 2 slope shallower.\n146\t  analysis: '2/3 seeds 完全 collapse（eval <145@45K + accelerating normalized v/e >2.0x），\n147\t    1 seed 显著 degradation 但未 crash（eval 162@45K, normalized v/e 1.66x 仍在 pathological\n148\t    zone 但增速慢）。 这支持 \"trained dt_emb is a primary contributing factor\" 而非 \"deterministic\n149\t    root cause\"。 normalized v/e >1.5x 在所有 3 seeds 出现，作为 diagnostic signal 仍然 robust。\n150\t\n151\t    '\n152\t- name: Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\n153\t  plan_id: plan_012\n154\t  description: 'Replicate causal control: subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8'\n155\t  expected_results:\n156\t    seed1_eval_return_25K: 185\n157\t    seed1_eval_return_35K: 195\n158\t    seed1_eval_return_55K: 215\n159\t    seed1_normalized_ve_25K: 0.98\n160\t    seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 0.78\n161\t    seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.7\n162\t    seed1_verdict: STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\n163\t    seed2_eval_return_25K: 175\n164\t    seed2_eval_return_35K: 190\n165\t    seed2_eval_return_55K: 200\n166\t    seed2_normalized_ve_25K: 1.08\n167\t    seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 0.85\n168\t    seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.82\n169\t    seed2_verdict: STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\n170\t    stable_replication_count: 3\n171\t    cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 207\n172\t    cross_seed_nve_range_55K: 0.70-0.82\n173\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档假设 008f 全程 stable（normalized v/e <1.1x）。 Seed 0 已确认 stable（nve\n174\t    1.02x@25K→0.73x@35K，下降趋势）。 移除 dt_embedding 后 value function 无法 exploit dt 信息，\n175\t    因此所有 seeds 都应显示 normalized v/e 收敛到 baseline 水平或以下。 Eval performance 受限于 H=8 +\n176\t    subsample ON（学习信号减少）， 停留在 baseline 的 ~20-22%，但关键是没有 collapse。 3/3 seeds stable\n177\t    是 median 档的合理预期——因为这是一个 \"移除有害因素\" 的实验， variance 主要体现在 absolute performance 而非 collapse/non-collapse\n178\t    的二分上。\n179\t\n180\t    '\n181\t  tables:\n182\t  - name: 008f stability replication (3 seeds)\n183\t    columns:\n184\t    - step\n185\t    - seed0_eval\n186\t    - seed1_eval\n187\t    - seed2_eval\n188\t    - seed0_nve\n189\t    - seed1_nve\n190\t    - seed2_nve\n191\t    rows:\n192\t    - - 25K\n193\t      - 197\n194\t      - 185\n195\t      - 175\n196\t      - 1.02\n197\t      - 0.98\n198\t      - 1.08\n199\t    - - 35K\n200\t      - 207\n201\t      - 195\n202\t      - 190\n203\t      - 0.73\n204\t      - 0.78\n205\t      - 0.85\n206\t    - - 55K\n207\t      - 210\n208\t      - 215\n209\t      - 200\n210\t      - 0.68\n211\t      - 0.7\n212\t      - 0.82\n213\t  figures_description:\n214\t  - 3-seed 008f learning curves. All slowly increasing, no collapse. Clear contrast\n215\t    with 008d.\n216\t  - '3-seed normalized v/e: all converge below 1.0x by 35K, confirming dt_embedding\n217\t    removal eliminates delusional critic.'\n218\t  analysis: '008f 的 3-seed stability 与 008d 的 2/3-seed collapse 形成鲜明对比。 因果推断仍然成立：在完全相同的\n219\t    subsample ON + H=8 条件下， 唯一差异（dt_embedding 有/无）决定了 collapse/stable 分野。 即使 008d\n220\t    seed 2 未完全 collapse，其 normalized v/e（1.52-1.66x） 与 008f 全部 seeds 的 nve（0.68-1.08x）之间有明确\n221\t    gap。\n222\t\n223\t    '\n224\t- name: Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\n225\t  plan_id: plan_013\n226\t  description: 'Replicate value growth suppression: subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb\n227\t    + H=15'\n228\t  expected_results:\n229\t    seed1_eval_return_55K: 510\n230\t    seed1_eval_return_65K: 580\n231\t    seed1_eval_return_85K: 550\n232\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 720\n233\t    seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.88\n234\t    seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.65\n235\t    seed1_v_recovery_cycles: 2\n236\t    seed1_verdict: V_RECOVERY_CONFIRMED\n237\t    seed2_eval_return_55K: 460\n238\t    seed2_eval_return_65K: 530\n239\t    seed2_eval_return_85K: 520\n240\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 580\n241\t    seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.95\n242\t    seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.78\n243\t    seed2_v_recovery_cycles: 0\n244\t    seed2_verdict: PLATEAU_NO_COLLAPSE\n245\t    recovery_replication_count: 2\n246\t    cross_seed_mean_105K: 693\n247\t    multiseed_mean_105K_range: 580-778\n248\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档假设：008a V-recovery 在 2/3 seeds 出现，1 seed 仅 plateau 不\n249\t    recover。 Seed 0 已确认双 V-recovery（501→608→470→778）。 Seed 1 预期类似 pattern：untrained\n250\t    dt_emb 抑制 value overestimation， 允许 actor 在过拟合后恢复，但 peak 略低于 seed 0（720 vs 778）。\n251\t    Seed 2 是 median 档的区分点——normalized v/e 仍被抑制（<1.0x，无 collapse）， 但 eval return 在\n252\t    530 附近 plateau 而非形成清晰 V-recovery。 可能机制：seed 2 的 actor 收敛到一个 suboptimal 但 stable\n253\t    的 policy， value suppression 阻止了 overestimation 但 exploration 不足以跳出 local optimum。\n254\t    关键是 3/3 seeds 都 no collapse + normalized v/e <1.0x， protective effect 是 robust\n255\t    的；V-recovery 的具体 pattern 有 seed variance。 cross_seed_mean_105K = (778+720+580)/3\n256\t    ≈ 693，落在 median 档指标范围 [550,720] 内。\n257\t\n258\t    '\n259\t  tables:\n260\t  - name: 008a V-recovery replication (3 seeds)\n261\t    columns:\n262\t    - step\n263\t    - seed0_eval\n264\t    - seed1_eval\n265\t    - seed2_eval\n266\t    - seed0_nve\n267\t    - seed1_nve\n268\t    - seed2_nve\n269\t    rows:\n270\t    - - 55K\n271\t      - 488\n272\t      - 510\n273\t      - 460\n274\t      - 0.93\n275\t      - 0.88\n276\t      - 0.95\n277\t    - - 65K\n278\t      - 608\n279\t      - 580\n280\t      - 530\n281\t      - 0.66\n282\t      - 0.72\n283\t      - 0.8\n284\t    - - 85K\n285\t      - 584\n286\t      - 550\n287\t      - 520\n288\t      - 0.68\n289\t      - 0.71\n290\t      - 0.76\n291\t    - - 105K\n292\t      - 778\n293\t      - 720\n294\t      - 580\n295\t      - 0.59\n296\t      - 0.65\n297\t      - 0.78\n298\t  figures_description:\n299\t  - 3-seed 008a learning curves. Seed 0,1 show V-shaped recoveries; seed 2 plateaus\n300\t    at ~530 without collapse.\n301\t  - '3-seed normalized v/e: all consistently <1.0x, confirming structural value suppression\n302\t    across seeds.'\n303\t  analysis: 'V-recovery 的 seed variance 迫使将 C3 的表述从 \"V-shaped recovery is a signature\"  调整为\n304\t    \"untrained dt_emb consistently prevents collapse and suppresses v/e,  with recovery\n305\t    dynamics varying across seeds\"。 核心 finding（value suppression → no collapse）在 3/3\n306\t    seeds robust。 V-recovery 作为 secondary pattern 在 2/3 seeds 出现，可作为 suggestive evidence\n307\t    而非 strong claim。\n308\t\n309\t    '\n310\t- name: Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\n311\t  plan_id: plan_020\n312\t  description: dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment, establishing Cheetah-specific\n313\t    v/e calibration\n314\t  expected_results:\n315\t    seed0_eval_return_55K: 450\n316\t    seed0_eval_return_105K: 680\n317\t    seed0_eval_return_asymptotic: 780\n318\t    seed1_eval_return_55K: 430\n319\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 660\n320\t    seed1_eval_return_asymptotic: 760\n321\t    seed2_eval_return_55K: 470\n322\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 700\n323\t    seed2_eval_return_asymptotic: 800\n324\t    mean_eval_return_asymptotic: 780\n325\t    mean_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.19\n326\t    mean_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.35\n327\t    mean_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.55\n328\t    ve_stable_range: 58-65%\n329\t  result_rationale: 'Cheetah Run 的 DreamerV3 baseline 通常低于 Walker Walk（~780 vs ~950）。\n330\t    Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更连续平滑（locomotion on flat terrain）， RSSM 对 Cheetah 的 reconstruction\n331\t    quality 通常优于 Walker（接触力学更简单）。 v/e 稳态 58-65% 略低于 Walker 的 69-72%，反映 Cheetah 的 reward\n332\t    landscape 不同。 3 seeds variance 预期 ±3-5%，略高于 Walker（Cheetah 的 reward 更连续 → 更多 local\n333\t    optima）。\n334\t\n335\t    '\n336\t  tables:\n337\t  - name: Cheetah Run baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\n338\t    columns:\n339\t    - step\n340\t    - mean_eval\n341\t    - std_eval\n342\t    - mean_ve\n343\t    - std_ve\n344\t    rows:\n345\t    - - 25K\n346\t      - 220\n347\t      - 25\n348\t      - 0.1\n349\t      - 0.02\n350\t    - - 35K\n351\t      - 310\n352\t      - 20\n353\t      - 0.19\n354\t      - 0.03\n355\t    - - 55K\n356\t      - 450\n357\t      - 20\n358\t      - 0.35\n359\t      - 0.03\n360\t    - - 105K\n361\t      - 680\n362\t      - 20\n363\t      - 0.55\n364\t      - 0.04\n365\t  figures_description:\n366\t  - Cheetah Run 3-seed baseline with shaded std. Slower initial learning than Walker,\n367\t    smooth convergence.\n368\t  - Cheetah v/e calibration curve. Same monotonic rise shape as Walker but lower asymptote\n369\t    (~60% vs ~70%).\n370\t  analysis: 'Cheetah baseline 的 v/e asymptote 较低（~60% vs Walker ~70%）， 这将影响 normalized\n371\t    v/e 的解读——同样的 absolute v/e 在 Cheetah 中 normalized 更高。 需要 environment-specific calibration，不能直接复用\n372\t    Walker 的 1.5x 阈值。\n373\t\n374\t    '\n375\t- name: Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n376\t  plan_id: plan_021\n377\t  description: 'Replicate delusional critic in Cheetah Run: dt=2 + subsample ON +\n378\t    trained dt_emb + H=8'\n379\t  expected_results:\n380\t    seed0_eval_return_25K: 160\n381\t    seed0_eval_return_35K: 200\n382\t    seed0_eval_return_45K: 195\n383\t    seed0_eval_return_55K: 180\n384\t    seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 1.35\n385\t    seed0_normalized_ve_45K: 1.45\n386\t    seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 1.5\n387\t    seed0_verdict: DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\n388\t    seed1_eval_return_35K: 220\n389\t    seed1_eval_return_55K: 205\n390\t    seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.25\n391\t    seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 1.38\n392\t    seed1_verdict: DEGRADATION_MILD\n393\t    seed2_eval_return_35K: 185\n394\t    seed2_eval_return_55K: 165\n395\t    seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.4\n396\t    seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 1.52\n397\t    seed2_verdict: DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\n398\t    cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 183\n399\t    cheetah_trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve: 1.35\n400\t    collapse_count: 0\n401\t    vs_baseline_pct_55K: -59%\n402\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：Cheetah Run 中 trained dt_emb 降性能但 collapse 不如 Walker\n403\t    剧烈 （normalized v/e 1.2-1.5x，边界区）。 机制：Cheetah 的 dynamics 比 Walker 更平滑连续，RSSM 在\n404\t    dt=2 的 prediction error 较低。 因此 trained dt_emb 导致的 value overestimation 速度更慢、幅度更小。\n405\t    normalized v/e 在 1.2-1.5x 区间——超过 baseline 但未达到 Walker 的 >2.0x 加速 diverge。 Eval\n406\t    return 呈缓慢下降趋势（200→180）而非 Walker 的急剧 collapse（167→141）。 这产生了关键的 \"environment-dependent\n407\t    modulation\" 叙事： 相同的 dt_embedding 机制在不同 RSSM fidelity 条件下产生不同严重程度。 从方法论看，这其实 *strengthens*\n408\t    而非 weakens 因果解释—— 因为它指向 RSSM prediction quality 作为调节变量，与 C2 机制一致。\n409\t\n410\t    '\n411\t  tables:\n412\t  - name: Cheetah trained dt_emb (3 seeds) vs Walker 008d\n413\t    columns:\n414\t    - env\n415\t    - step\n416\t    - mean_eval\n417\t    - mean_nve\n418\t    - walker_008d_nve\n419\t    - gap\n420\t    rows:\n421\t    - - Cheetah\n422\t      - 25K\n423\t      - 170\n424\t      - 1.2\n425\t      - 1.78\n426\t      - -0.58x\n427\t    - - Cheetah\n428\t      - 35K\n429\t      - 202\n430\t      - 1.33\n431\t      - 1.71\n432\t      - -0.38x\n433\t    - - Cheetah\n434\t      - 45K\n435\t      - 195\n436\t      - 1.42\n437\t      - 2.09\n438\t      - -0.67x\n439\t    - - Cheetah\n440\t      - 55K\n441\t      - 183\n442\t      - 1.47\n443\t      - N/A (collapsed)\n444\t      - —\n445\t  figures_description:\n446\t  - Cheetah trained dt_emb 3-seed curves vs Cheetah baseline. Degradation visible\n447\t    but no sharp collapse.\n448\t  - 'Cross-environment normalized v/e comparison: Walker 008d (accelerating >2.0x)\n449\t    vs Cheetah (plateau ~1.3-1.5x).'\n450\t  analysis: 'Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb 效果是 \"attenuated Walker\" 而非 \"clean replication\"。\n451\t    这是 median 档的核心挑战：collapse 不复现，但 degradation 和 elevated v/e 复现。 需要 reframe C2：dt_embedding\n452\t    的危害程度由 RSSM fidelity at dt>1 调节。 Walker 的 contact dynamics → 高 RSSM error → 快速\n453\t    collapse。 Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics → 低 RSSM error → 慢速 degradation。 v/e overshoot\n454\t    ratio >1.5x 阈值在 Cheetah 中不是硬界限而是 \"warning zone\"。\n455\t\n456\t    '\n457\t- name: Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n458\t  plan_id: plan_022\n459\t  description: 'Causal control in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 +\n460\t    H=8'\n461\t  expected_results:\n462\t    seed0_eval_return_35K: 195\n463\t    seed0_eval_return_55K: 220\n464\t    seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 0.82\n465\t    seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 0.75\n466\t    seed1_eval_return_55K: 210\n467\t    seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.8\n468\t    seed2_eval_return_55K: 230\n469\t    seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.72\n470\t    cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 220\n471\t    cross_seed_mean_nve_55K: 0.76\n472\t    cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve: 0.76\n473\t    vs_baseline_pct_55K: -51%\n474\t    vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_eval: +37 (220 vs 183)\n475\t    vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_nve: -0.71x (0.76 vs 1.47)\n476\t  result_rationale: '移除 dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中同样消除 elevated v/e，但 performance gap\n477\t    较 Walker 小。 在 Walker 中，008f vs 008d 的 eval gap 明显（207 vs 141@55K）。 在 Cheetah 中，gap\n478\t    缩小（220 vs 183@55K），因为 baseline degradation 本身较温和。 Normalized v/e 在 0.7-1.15x 范围（median\n479\t    档指标），低于 1.0x 表示 no overestimation。 因果方向仍一致（有 dt_emb → nve>1.2x, 无 dt_emb → nve<1.0x），但\n480\t    effect size 较小。 这支持 \"dt_embedding is harmful but severity is environment-modulated\"。\n481\t\n482\t    '\n483\t  tables:\n484\t  - name: Cheetah 008f-equivalent vs trained dt_emb (mean across 3 seeds)\n485\t    columns:\n486\t    - config\n487\t    - eval_55K\n488\t    - nve_55K\n489\t    - collapse\n490\t    rows:\n491\t    - - trained dt_emb\n492\t      - 183\n493\t      - 1.47\n494\t      - degradation (no collapse)\n495\t    - - dt_embed_dim=0\n496\t      - 220\n497\t      - 0.76\n498\t      - no degradation\n499\t    - - baseline\n500\t      - 450\n501\t      - 1.0 (reference)\n502\t      - N/A\n503\t  figures_description:\n504\t  - 'Cheetah causal comparison: trained dt_emb (declining, elevated nve) vs dt_embed_dim=0\n505\t    (stable, suppressed nve).'\n506\t  analysis: '因果方向在 Cheetah 仍成立（removing dt_emb → lower v/e + better performance），\n507\t    但 effect size 是 Walker 的约 50%。这是论文中 \"boundary conditions\" section 的核心数据： 当 RSSM\n508\t    prediction quality 较好时（Cheetah），dt_embedding 的危害减轻但不消失。 cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve=0.76\n509\t    落在 median 档指标范围 [0.7, 1.15] 内。\n510\t\n511\t    '\n512\t- name: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\n513\t  plan_id: plan_023\n514\t  description: 'Value growth suppression in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample OFF + untrained\n515\t    dt_emb + H=15'\n516\t  expected_results:\n517\t    seed0_eval_return_55K: 380\n518\t    seed0_eval_return_105K: 550\n519\t    seed0_normalized_ve_105K: 0.72\n520\t    seed1_eval_return_105K: 520\n521\t    seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.78\n522\t    seed2_eval_return_105K: 490\n523\t    seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.82\n524\t    cross_seed_mean_105K: 520\n525\t    vs_baseline_pct_105K: -24%\n526\t    v_recovery_count: 1/3 seeds shows V-recovery, 2/3 plateau\n527\t    cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct: 67%\n528\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档假设：Cheetah 中 untrained dt_emb 有保护作用但 gap 较小。 Walker 中\n529\t    008a 达 baseline 85%（778/916），Cheetah 预期只达 67%（520/780）。 原因：Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics\n530\t    使 RSSM error 较低 → trained dt_emb 的危害本就较小 →  untrained dt_emb 的 \"保护效果\" 相对 margin\n531\t    也较小（从 183 到 220 vs 从 141 到 207 in Walker）。 V-recovery pattern 在 Cheetah 中更弱：只有\n532\t    1/3 seeds 出现， 因为 Cheetah 的 reward landscape 更平 → actor 倾向 plateau 而非 oscillate。\n533\t    cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct=67% 落在 median 档指标范围 [50%, 75%] 内。\n534\t\n535\t    '\n536\t  tables:\n537\t  - name: Cheetah untrained dt_emb recovery (3 seeds)\n538\t    columns:\n539\t    - step\n540\t    - seed0\n541\t    - seed1\n542\t    - seed2\n543\t    - mean\n544\t    - nve_mean\n545\t    rows:\n546\t    - - 55K\n547\t      - 380\n548\t      - 360\n549\t      - 350\n550\t      - 363\n551\t      - 0.88\n552\t    - - 75K\n553\t      - 420\n554\t      - 440\n555\t      - 410\n556\t      - 423\n557\t      - 0.82\n558\t    - - 105K\n559\t      - 550\n560\t      - 520\n561\t      - 490\n562\t      - 520\n563\t      - 0.77\n564\t  figures_description:\n565\t  - Cheetah 008a-equivalent 3-seed curves. Slow monotonic improvement, fewer oscillations\n566\t    than Walker.\n567\t  - 'Cross-environment untrained dt_emb comparison: Walker shows V-recovery, Cheetah\n568\t    shows plateau-rise.'\n569\t  analysis: 'Cheetah 的 untrained dt_emb configuration 确认 protective effect（no collapse,\n570\t    nve<1.0x） 但 recovery 更缓慢。这与 environment-dependent modulation 假设一致： Cheetah 的 RSSM\n571\t    error 较低 → dt_emb 的影响（有害或保护性的）都被 attenuate。 论文中可用此数据支持 \"the dt_embedding mechanism\n572\t    is general,  but its magnitude scales with RSSM prediction error\"。\n573\t\n574\t    '\n575\t- name: 'RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions'\n576\t  plan_id: plan_030\n577\t  description: Measure observation/reward reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1 from\n578\t    existing trained models across both environments\n579\t  expected_results:\n580\t    walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt1: 4.2\n581\t    walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt2: 6.8\n582\t    walker_dt2_dt1_ratio: 1.62\n583\t    cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt1: 3.9\n584\t    cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt2: 5.1\n585\t    cheetah_dt2_dt1_ratio: 1.31\n586\t    walker_reward_pred_error_dt1: 0.08\n587\t    walker_reward_pred_error_dt2: 0.25\n588\t    cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt1: 0.06\n589\t    cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt2: 0.12\n590\t    cross_env_recon_gap_ratio: 1.24\n591\t  result_rationale: '这是 median 档叙事的关键支撑实验——直接量化 RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment dependence。\n592\t    Walker Walk 涉及 contact dynamics（脚与地面碰撞），dt=2 跳过一个接触事件时 RSSM 需要 \"想象\" 中间状态，reconstruction\n593\t    loss 预期升高 ~60%（ratio 1.6x）。 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更平滑（无离散接触切换）， dt=2 的 prediction\n594\t    误差增幅较小（~30%, ratio 1.3x）。 这个 1.6x vs 1.3x 的差距直接解释了为什么 trained dt_emb 在 Walker\n595\t    导致 collapse  而在 Cheetah 仅导致 degradation：更大的 RSSM error → 更多 delusional critic\n596\t    gradient → 更快 collapse。 Reward prediction error 的环境间差异更大（3.1x vs 2.0x ratio），\n597\t    因为 Walker 的 reward 与接触事件强耦合。\n598\t\n599\t    '\n600\t  tables:\n601\t  - name: 'RSSM reconstruction loss: dt=1 vs dt=2 × environment'\n602\t    columns:\n603\t    - environment\n604\t    - loss_dt1\n605\t    - loss_dt2\n606\t    - ratio\n607\t    - reward_err_dt1\n608\t    - reward_err_dt2\n609\t    - reward_ratio\n610\t    rows:\n611\t    - - Walker Walk\n612\t      - 4.2\n613\t      - 6.8\n614\t      - 1.62\n615\t      - 0.08\n616\t      - 0.25\n617\t      - 3.13\n618\t    - - Cheetah Run\n619\t      - 3.9\n620\t      - 5.1\n621\t      - 1.31\n622\t      - 0.06\n623\t      - 0.12\n624\t      - 2.0\n625\t  figures_description:\n626\t  - 'Bar chart: RSSM reconstruction loss at dt=1 vs dt=2 for both environments. Walker\n627\t    gap visibly larger.'\n628\t  - 'Scatter: RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio (x) vs peak normalized v/e in trained dt_emb config\n629\t    (y). Two points but on the expected trend line.'\n630\t  analysis: 'plan_030 提供了 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 假设的 mechanistic foundation。\n631\t    Walker 的 RSSM dt2/dt1 gap 比 Cheetah 大 ~24%（1.62/1.31=1.24x）， 这与 Walker 中 trained\n632\t    dt_emb 导致更严重 collapse 的观察一致。 但只有两个环境点，无法建立 quantitative 关系。 论文中应呈现为 \"consistent\n633\t    with the hypothesis\" 而非 \"proves\"。 如果 plan_040（Hopper Hop）执行，将提供第三个点。\n634\t\n635\t    '\n636\t- name: Actor entropy analysis\n637\t  plan_id: plan_031\n638\t  description: Plot actor entropy vs training step for healthy (008a/008c/008f) vs\n639\t    collapsed (006/008d) configurations\n640\t  expected_results:\n641\t    walker_008d_entropy_25K: 3.8\n642\t    walker_008d_entropy_35K: 4.1\n643\t    walker_008d_entropy_45K: 4.5\n644\t    walker_008d_entropy_trend: increasing\n645\t    walker_006_entropy_35K: 3.9\n646\t    walker_006_entropy_55K: 5.2\n647\t    walker_006_entropy_trend: sharply_increasing\n648\t    walker_008a_entropy_55K: 3.2\n649\t    walker_008a_entropy_105K: 2.8\n650\t    walker_008a_entropy_trend: stable_to_decreasing\n651\t    walker_008f_entropy_35K: 3.5\n652\t    walker_008f_entropy_trend: stable\n653\t    walker_baseline_entropy_35K: 3.0\n654\t    walker_baseline_entropy_105K: 2.5\n655\t    walker_baseline_entropy_trend: decreasing\n656\t  result_rationale: 'Actor entropy 增高表示 policy 变得更随机——这是 delusional critic gradient\n657\t    的下游症状。 当 value function 高估 → actor 收到 misleading gradient → policy 不再有 clear preference\n658\t    → entropy 升高。 预期 collapsed configs（008d, 006）显示 entropy 单调上升（actor confusion），\n659\t    而 healthy configs（008a, 008f, baseline）显示 entropy stable 或下降（policy sharpening）。\n660\t    这不是新发现，但提供了 mechanism 的额外 sanity check： 如果 collapsed configs 的 entropy *不*上升，则\n661\t    C2 的 \"delusional critic → actor degradation\" 链需要修正。 Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 noise\n662\t    较大（因为 entropy 是 high-variance metric）。\n663\t\n664\t    '\n665\t  tables:\n666\t  - name: Actor entropy trajectories\n667\t    columns:\n668\t    - config\n669\t    - entropy_25K\n670\t    - entropy_35K\n671\t    - entropy_45K\n672\t    - entropy_55K\n673\t    - trend\n674\t    rows:\n675\t    - - baseline\n676\t      - 3.2\n677\t      - 3.0\n678\t      - 2.9\n679\t      - 2.8\n680\t      - decreasing\n681\t    - - 008d (collapse)\n682\t      - 3.8\n683\t      - 4.1\n684\t      - 4.5\n685\t      - —\n686\t      - increasing\n687\t    - - 006 (collapse)\n688\t      - 3.5\n689\t      - 3.9\n690\t      - 4.2\n691\t      - 5.2\n692\t      - sharply increasing\n693\t    - - 008a (V-recovery)\n694\t      - 3.3\n695\t      - 3.1\n696\t      - 3.0\n697\t      - 3.2\n698\t      - stable\n699\t    - - 008f (stable)\n700\t      - 3.4\n701\t      - 3.5\n702\t      - 3.3\n703\t      - —\n704\t      - stable\n705\t  figures_description:\n706\t  - 'Actor entropy over training: collapsed configs diverge upward, healthy configs\n707\t    converge downward. Clear separation after 25K.'\n708\t  analysis: 'Entropy analysis 为 C2 提供 corroborating evidence 而非 primary evidence。\n709\t    Collapsed configs 的 entropy 上升模式与 \"delusional critic → actor confusion\" 一致。 在\n710\t    paper 中作为 supplementary figure 或 appendix，支撑 main text 的 causal diagram。\n711\t\n712\t    '\n713\t- name: Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\n714\t  plan_id: plan_032\n715\t  description: Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return for trained vs untrained\n716\t    dt_emb\n717\t  expected_results:\n718\t    walker_008d_value_mc_correlation: 0.35\n719\t    walker_008d_value_bias: +45% (systematic overestimation)\n720\t    walker_008d_value_std_ratio: 2.1\n721\t    walker_008a_value_mc_correlation: 0.72\n722\t    walker_008a_value_bias: +8% (mild overestimation)\n723\t    walker_008a_value_std_ratio: 1.2\n724\t    walker_baseline_value_mc_correlation: 0.85\n725\t    walker_baseline_value_bias: +5%\n726\t    walker_baseline_value_std_ratio: 1.1\n727\t    walker_008f_value_mc_correlation: 0.68\n728\t    walker_008f_value_bias: +10%\n729\t    walker_008f_value_std_ratio: 1.3\n730\t  result_rationale: 'V(s) vs MC return 的联合分布揭示 v/e ratio 无法捕捉的细节。 008d（trained dt_emb,\n731\t    collapse）预期显示：(a) systematic positive bias（值线远高于 y=x）， (b) 低相关性（value 与实际 return\n732\t    decouple），(c) 高 variance ratio（value 在不确定状态大幅波动）。 这三个特征共同构成 \"delusional critic\"\n733\t    的 distributional fingerprint。 008a/008f（healthy configs）预期接近 baseline 分布，bias\n734\t    小、相关性高。 Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 008f 的 correlation 略低于 baseline （因为 dt=2 imagination\n735\t    本身引入了一些 noise，即使没有 dt_embedding）。\n736\t\n737\t    '\n738\t  tables:\n739\t  - name: Value calibration summary\n740\t    columns:\n741\t    - config\n742\t    - correlation\n743\t    - bias_pct\n744\t    - variance_ratio\n745\t    - verdict\n746\t    rows:\n747\t    - - baseline\n748\t      - 0.85\n749\t      - +5%\n750\t      - 1.1\n751\t      - calibrated\n752\t    - - 008a (untrained)\n753\t      - 0.72\n754\t      - +8%\n755\t      - 1.2\n756\t      - mildly_optimistic\n757\t    - - 008f (no dt_emb)\n758\t      - 0.68\n759\t      - +10%\n760\t      - 1.3\n761\t      - mildly_optimistic\n762\t    - - 008d (trained)\n763\t      - 0.35\n764\t      - +45%\n765\t      - 2.1\n766\t      - delusional\n767\t  figures_description:\n768\t  - '2×2 scatter plot grid: V(s) vs MC return for baseline, 008a, 008f, 008d. Each\n769\t    with y=x line and regression fit.'\n770\t  - 'Histogram: value prediction error distribution (V(s) - MC) for each config. 008d\n771\t    shows heavy right tail.'\n772\t  analysis: 'Distribution analysis 将 v/e ratio proxy 升级为更 rigorous 的 value calibration\n773\t    证据。 008d 的 correlation=0.35 和 bias=+45% 直接证明 \"delusional\"——value function 的预测\n774\t    与实际 return 几乎 decouple 且系统性偏高。 这是 paper 中最强的 supplementary evidence，值得在 main text\n775\t    中给一段或一个 figure。\n776\t\n777\t    '\n778\t- name: dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\n779\t  plan_id: plan_033\n780\t  description: 'Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors: cosine similarity between dt=1\n781\t    and dt=2'\n782\t  expected_results:\n783\t    cosine_sim_5K: 0.92\n784\t    cosine_sim_15K: 0.75\n785\t    cosine_sim_35K: 0.42\n786\t    cosine_sim_55K: 0.28\n787\t    embedding_norm_dt1_35K: 1.2\n788\t    embedding_norm_dt2_35K: 2.8\n789\t    embedding_divergence_onset: ~15K-25K (coincides with v/e acceleration)\n790\t  result_rationale: 'Trained dt_embedding 在训练过程中逐步学会区分 dt=1 和 dt=2。 早期（<10K）dt=1 和\n791\t    dt=2 embedding 相似（cosine~0.9），value function 尚未 exploit 差异。 15-25K 时 embedding\n792\t    开始分离（cosine 下降到 0.5-0.7）， 这恰好与 v/e ratio 开始加速的时间窗口吻合。 这提供了 temporal evidence：dt_embedding\n793\t    的学习 → value function 开始 exploit → overestimation → collapse。 dt=2 embedding 的\n794\t    norm 增大（2.8 vs dt=1 的 1.2）表明 value function 放大了 dt=2 的表征， 可能因为 dt=2 transition\n795\t    在 imagination 中产生更大的 \"value opportunity\"（但实际是虚假的）。\n796\t\n797\t    '\n798\t  tables:\n799\t  - name: dt_embedding evolution during training\n800\t    columns:\n801\t    - step\n802\t    - cosine_sim\n803\t    - norm_dt1\n804\t    - norm_dt2\n805\t    - nve_at_step\n806\t    rows:\n807\t    - - 5K\n808\t      - 0.92\n809\t      - 0.8\n810\t      - 0.9\n811\t      - ~1.0x\n812\t    - - 15K\n813\t      - 0.75\n814\t      - 1.0\n815\t      - 1.4\n816\t      - ~1.2x\n817\t    - - 25K\n818\t      - 0.55\n819\t      - 1.1\n820\t      - 2.1\n821\t      - ~1.5x\n822\t    - - 35K\n823\t      - 0.42\n824\t      - 1.2\n825\t      - 2.8\n826\t      - ~1.7x\n827\t  figures_description:\n828\t  - 'Dual-axis plot: cosine similarity (decreasing) and normalized v/e (increasing)\n829\t    vs training step. Divergence onset co-occurs.'\n830\t  - 2D PCA of dt_embedding at [5K, 15K, 25K, 35K]. dt=1 and dt=2 clusters separate\n831\t    over training.\n832\t  analysis: 'Cosine similarity 分析提供 mechanistic timeline：embedding 分离 → value exploitation\n833\t    → collapse。 这是 P2 priority 因为它补充而非替代 core evidence， 但在论文中可以做一个很有说服力的 timeline\n834\t    figure。 如果 embedding 的分离时间与 v/e 加速不吻合，则 C2 的 mechanism story 需要修正。\n835\t\n836\t    '\n837\t- name: Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\n838\t  plan_id: plan_040\n839\t  description: 'Third DMC environment: baseline + trained dt_emb + dt_embed_dim=0'\n840\t  expected_results:\n841\t    baseline_asymptotic: 250\n842\t    trained_dtEmb_peak: 120\n843\t    trained_dtEmb_nve_peak: 1.55\n844\t    trained_dtEmb_collapse: partial (1/3 seeds collapse, 2/3 degradation)\n845\t    no_dtEmb_eval_55K: 105\n846\t    no_dtEmb_nve_55K: 0.85\n847\t    baseline_ve_stable: 55-62%\n848\t  result_rationale: 'Hopper Hop 是高难度 DMC task（baseline ~250 远低于 Walker ~950 和 Cheetah\n849\t    ~780）。 RSSM prediction quality 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间 （有 hopping contact events\n850\t    但比 walking 更规律）。 Median 档下预期 trained dt_emb 的 normalized v/e 在 Walker 和 Cheetah\n851\t    之间（~1.5x）， 1/3 seeds collapse，2/3 degradation。 dt_embed_dim=0 仍应 stable（nve <1.0x）。\n852\t    但 Hopper 的 absolute performance 很低，signal-to-noise ratio 差 →  结论 less conclusive，主要价值是提供\n853\t    plan_030 scatter plot 的第三个点。 P2 priority，论文如时间不够可省略。\n854\t\n855\t    '\n856\t  tables:\n857\t  - name: Hopper Hop results summary\n858\t    columns:\n859\t    - config\n860\t    - mean_eval_55K\n861\t    - mean_nve_55K\n862\t    - collapse_fraction\n863\t    rows:\n864\t    - - baseline\n865\t      - 180\n866\t      - 1.0 (ref)\n867\t      - 0/3\n868\t    - - trained dt_emb\n869\t      - 95\n870\t      - 1.55\n871\t      - 1/3\n872\t    - - dt_embed_dim=0\n873\t      - 105\n874\t      - 0.85\n875\t      - 0/3\n876\t  figures_description:\n877\t  - 'Three-environment summary: RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio vs peak normalized v/e. Three points\n878\t    showing positive trend.'\n879\t  analysis: Hopper 作为第三环境，主要贡献是验证 environment-dependent modulation 假设。 如果 RSSM dt2/dt1\n880\t    ratio 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（如 plan_030 预测）， 且 normalized v/e 也介于两者之间，则三个点落在一条正相关趋势线上——\n881\t    这将 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 从 post-hoc 假设升级为 empirical pattern。 但 P2\n882\t    priority 意味着在 CoRL deadline 前可能无法完成。 Median 档论文即使没有 Hopper 也可以成立，用 Discussion\n883\t    中的 \"boundary conditions\" 段覆盖。\n884\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a90c8859-8e50-4bd7-a75e-c4f31c8dbc1b","uuid":"307175e7-c11e-4b56-a069-9ef3f94604d1","timestamp":"2026-05-14T07:01:28.451Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T062606/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '因果诊断在 Walker Walk 仍成立但需加 nuance。标题用 \"Diagnosing Value Overestimation\n  in Temporally-Abstract World Models\"。 C2 措辞从 \"root cause\" 调为 \"primary contributing\n  factor in Walker Walk\"。 Cheetah Run 引入 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 讨论——RSSM\n  prediction error 的环境依赖性调节 dt_embedding 危害程度。 v/e overshoot ratio 从硬规则降为启发式。Discussion\n  增加 \"boundary conditions\" 分析。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 2 additional seeds for dt=1 baseline, establishing per-seed v/e calibration\n    curves\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_eval_return_55K: 610\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 890\n    seed1_eval_return_last10_mean: 935\n    seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.255\n    seed1_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.42\n    seed1_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.67\n    seed2_eval_return_55K: 580\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 870\n    seed2_eval_return_last10_mean: 920\n    seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.22\n    seed2_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.38\n    seed2_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.64\n    cross_seed_mean_last10: 935\n    cross_seed_std_last10: 15\n    cross_seed_ve_stable_range: 67-74%\n  result_rationale: 'Walker Walk dt=1 baseline 在 DreamerV3 中是成熟配置，seed 间 variance\n    较小。 Seed 0 asymptote 950.9，预期 seed 1-2 在 920-950 范围内（±3%），v/e 稳态在 67-74%。 这是 median\n    档的正常 baseline variance，不影响因果链判断。 v/e calibration curves 形状一致（单调上升后饱和），但具体数值有 ±0.03\n    偏移， 这会为后续 normalized v/e 计算引入小幅 per-seed 校准差异。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\n    columns:\n    - step\n    - seed0_ve\n    - seed1_ve\n    - seed2_ve\n    - mean_ve\n    - std_ve\n    rows:\n    - - 25K\n      - 0.087\n      - 0.095\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.087\n      - 0.006\n    - - 35K\n      - 0.241\n      - 0.255\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.239\n      - 0.014\n    - - 55K\n      - 0.404\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.401\n      - 0.016\n    - - 105K\n      - 0.656\n      - 0.67\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.655\n      - 0.012\n  figures_description:\n  - 3-seed baseline learning curves (eval return vs step), shaded std band. All converge\n    to ~920-950 by 200K.\n  - 3-seed v/e ratio curves overlaid. Near-identical shape, stable from 135K+.\n  analysis: 'Baseline 的 3-seed 一致性高（CV<2%），为 normalized v/e 的 per-seed 计算提供可靠参考。 v/e\n    stable range 67-74% 跨 seed，比单 seed 的 69-72% 稍宽，但仍是紧致分布。 这意味着 >1.5x normalized\n    v/e 阈值在 3-seed 下仍有足够 margin。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 'Replicate delusional critic collapse: subsample ON + trained dt_emb\n    + H=8'\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_eval_return_25K: 155\n    seed1_eval_return_35K: 138\n    seed1_eval_return_45K: 125\n    seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.45\n    seed1_value_eval_ratio_45K: 0.72\n    seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.76\n    seed1_normalized_ve_45K: 2.17\n    seed1_verdict: COLLAPSE_CONFIRMED\n    seed2_eval_return_25K: 180\n    seed2_eval_return_35K: 170\n    seed2_eval_return_45K: 162\n    seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.35\n    seed2_value_eval_ratio_45K: 0.55\n    seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.59\n    seed2_normalized_ve_45K: 1.66\n    seed2_verdict: DEGRADATION_NO_FULL_COLLAPSE\n    collapse_replication_count: 2\n    cross_seed_mean_eval_45K: 143\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：008d collapse 在 2/3 seeds 复现，1 seed 仅 degradation\n    不 collapse。 Seed 0 已确认 collapse（eval 167→146→141, normalized v/e 1.78x→2.09x）。\n    Seed 1 预期复现类似 pattern：v/e 加速 diverge，eval 持续下降，构成 collapse。 Seed 2 是 median 档的关键区分点——trained\n    dt_emb 仍导致 elevated normalized v/e（>1.5x）， 但 eval 仅从 180 缓降到 162 而非 crash，v/e\n    加速率较低。 可能原因：seed 2 的 RSSM 恰好在 dt=2 transition 上学到了稍好的 representation， 使 value\n    overestimation 速度放慢但不消除。这给了足够 signal 说 trained dt_emb 有害， 但 variance 阻止了 \"100%\n    collapse\" 的强结论，需用 \"primary contributing factor\" 措辞。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 008d collapse replication (3 seeds)\n    columns:\n    - step\n    - seed0_eval\n    - seed1_eval\n    - seed2_eval\n    - seed0_nve\n    - seed1_nve\n    - seed2_nve\n    rows:\n    - - 25K\n      - 167\n      - 155\n      - 180\n      - 1.78\n      - 1.73\n      - 1.52\n    - - 35K\n      - 146\n      - 138\n      - 170\n      - 1.71\n      - 1.76\n      - 1.59\n    - - 45K\n      - 141\n      - 125\n      - 162\n      - 2.09\n      - 2.17\n      - 1.66\n  figures_description:\n  - 3-seed 008d learning curves. Seed 0,1 show clear collapse; seed 2 shows degradation\n    with slower decline.\n  - 3-seed normalized v/e trajectories. All >1.5x, but seed 2 slope shallower.\n  analysis: '2/3 seeds 完全 collapse（eval <145@45K + accelerating normalized v/e >2.0x），\n    1 seed 显著 degradation 但未 crash（eval 162@45K, normalized v/e 1.66x 仍在 pathological\n    zone 但增速慢）。 这支持 \"trained dt_emb is a primary contributing factor\" 而非 \"deterministic\n    root cause\"。 normalized v/e >1.5x 在所有 3 seeds 出现，作为 diagnostic signal 仍然 robust。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: 'Replicate causal control: subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8'\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_eval_return_25K: 185\n    seed1_eval_return_35K: 195\n    seed1_eval_return_55K: 215\n    seed1_normalized_ve_25K: 0.98\n    seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 0.78\n    seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.7\n    seed1_verdict: STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\n    seed2_eval_return_25K: 175\n    seed2_eval_return_35K: 190\n    seed2_eval_return_55K: 200\n    seed2_normalized_ve_25K: 1.08\n    seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 0.85\n    seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.82\n    seed2_verdict: STABLE_NO_COLLAPSE\n    stable_replication_count: 3\n    cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 207\n    cross_seed_nve_range_55K: 0.70-0.82\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档假设 008f 全程 stable（normalized v/e <1.1x）。 Seed 0 已确认 stable（nve\n    1.02x@25K→0.73x@35K，下降趋势）。 移除 dt_embedding 后 value function 无法 exploit dt 信息，\n    因此所有 seeds 都应显示 normalized v/e 收敛到 baseline 水平或以下。 Eval performance 受限于 H=8 +\n    subsample ON（学习信号减少）， 停留在 baseline 的 ~20-22%，但关键是没有 collapse。 3/3 seeds stable\n    是 median 档的合理预期——因为这是一个 \"移除有害因素\" 的实验， variance 主要体现在 absolute performance 而非 collapse/non-collapse\n    的二分上。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 008f stability replication (3 seeds)\n    columns:\n    - step\n    - seed0_eval\n    - seed1_eval\n    - seed2_eval\n    - seed0_nve\n    - seed1_nve\n    - seed2_nve\n    rows:\n    - - 25K\n      - 197\n      - 185\n      - 175\n      - 1.02\n      - 0.98\n      - 1.08\n    - - 35K\n      - 207\n      - 195\n      - 190\n      - 0.73\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.85\n    - - 55K\n      - 210\n      - 215\n      - 200\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.82\n  figures_description:\n  - 3-seed 008f learning curves. All slowly increasing, no collapse. Clear contrast\n    with 008d.\n  - '3-seed normalized v/e: all converge below 1.0x by 35K, confirming dt_embedding\n    removal eliminates delusional critic.'\n  analysis: '008f 的 3-seed stability 与 008d 的 2/3-seed collapse 形成鲜明对比。 因果推断仍然成立：在完全相同的\n    subsample ON + H=8 条件下， 唯一差异（dt_embedding 有/无）决定了 collapse/stable 分野。 即使 008d\n    seed 2 未完全 collapse，其 normalized v/e（1.52-1.66x） 与 008f 全部 seeds 的 nve（0.68-1.08x）之间有明确\n    gap。\n\n    '\n- name: Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: 'Replicate value growth suppression: subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb\n    + H=15'\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_eval_return_55K: 510\n    seed1_eval_return_65K: 580\n    seed1_eval_return_85K: 550\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 720\n    seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.88\n    seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.65\n    seed1_v_recovery_cycles: 2\n    seed1_verdict: V_RECOVERY_CONFIRMED\n    seed2_eval_return_55K: 460\n    seed2_eval_return_65K: 530\n    seed2_eval_return_85K: 520\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 580\n    seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.95\n    seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.78\n    seed2_v_recovery_cycles: 0\n    seed2_verdict: PLATEAU_NO_COLLAPSE\n    recovery_replication_count: 2\n    cross_seed_mean_105K: 693\n    multiseed_mean_105K_range: 580-778\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档假设：008a V-recovery 在 2/3 seeds 出现，1 seed 仅 plateau 不\n    recover。 Seed 0 已确认双 V-recovery（501→608→470→778）。 Seed 1 预期类似 pattern：untrained\n    dt_emb 抑制 value overestimation， 允许 actor 在过拟合后恢复，但 peak 略低于 seed 0（720 vs 778）。\n    Seed 2 是 median 档的区分点——normalized v/e 仍被抑制（<1.0x，无 collapse）， 但 eval return 在\n    530 附近 plateau 而非形成清晰 V-recovery。 可能机制：seed 2 的 actor 收敛到一个 suboptimal 但 stable\n    的 policy， value suppression 阻止了 overestimation 但 exploration 不足以跳出 local optimum。\n    关键是 3/3 seeds 都 no collapse + normalized v/e <1.0x， protective effect 是 robust\n    的；V-recovery 的具体 pattern 有 seed variance。 cross_seed_mean_105K = (778+720+580)/3\n    ≈ 693，落在 median 档指标范围 [550,720] 内。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 008a V-recovery replication (3 seeds)\n    columns:\n    - step\n    - seed0_eval\n    - seed1_eval\n    - seed2_eval\n    - seed0_nve\n    - seed1_nve\n    - seed2_nve\n    rows:\n    - - 55K\n      - 488\n      - 510\n      - 460\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.88\n      - 0.95\n    - - 65K\n      - 608\n      - 580\n      - 530\n      - 0.66\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.8\n    - - 85K\n      - 584\n      - 550\n      - 520\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.76\n    - - 105K\n      - 778\n      - 720\n      - 580\n      - 0.59\n      - 0.65\n      - 0.78\n  figures_description:\n  - 3-seed 008a learning curves. Seed 0,1 show V-shaped recoveries; seed 2 plateaus\n    at ~530 without collapse.\n  - '3-seed normalized v/e: all consistently <1.0x, confirming structural value suppression\n    across seeds.'\n  analysis: 'V-recovery 的 seed variance 迫使将 C3 的表述从 \"V-shaped recovery is a signature\"  调整为\n    \"untrained dt_emb consistently prevents collapse and suppresses v/e,  with recovery\n    dynamics varying across seeds\"。 核心 finding（value suppression → no collapse）在 3/3\n    seeds robust。 V-recovery 作为 secondary pattern 在 2/3 seeds 出现，可作为 suggestive evidence\n    而非 strong claim。\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_020\n  description: dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment, establishing Cheetah-specific\n    v/e calibration\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_return_55K: 450\n    seed0_eval_return_105K: 680\n    seed0_eval_return_asymptotic: 780\n    seed1_eval_return_55K: 430\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 660\n    seed1_eval_return_asymptotic: 760\n    seed2_eval_return_55K: 470\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 700\n    seed2_eval_return_asymptotic: 800\n    mean_eval_return_asymptotic: 780\n    mean_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.19\n    mean_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.35\n    mean_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.55\n    ve_stable_range: 58-65%\n  result_rationale: 'Cheetah Run 的 DreamerV3 baseline 通常低于 Walker Walk（~780 vs ~950）。\n    Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更连续平滑（locomotion on flat terrain）， RSSM 对 Cheetah 的 reconstruction\n    quality 通常优于 Walker（接触力学更简单）。 v/e 稳态 58-65% 略低于 Walker 的 69-72%，反映 Cheetah 的 reward\n    landscape 不同。 3 seeds variance 预期 ±3-5%，略高于 Walker（Cheetah 的 reward 更连续 → 更多 local\n    optima）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cheetah Run baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\n    columns:\n    - step\n    - mean_eval\n    - std_eval\n    - mean_ve\n    - std_ve\n    rows:\n    - - 25K\n      - 220\n      - 25\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.02\n    - - 35K\n      - 310\n      - 20\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.03\n    - - 55K\n      - 450\n      - 20\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.03\n    - - 105K\n      - 680\n      - 20\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.04\n  figures_description:\n  - Cheetah Run 3-seed baseline with shaded std. Slower initial learning than Walker,\n    smooth convergence.\n  - Cheetah v/e calibration curve. Same monotonic rise shape as Walker but lower asymptote\n    (~60% vs ~70%).\n  analysis: 'Cheetah baseline 的 v/e asymptote 较低（~60% vs Walker ~70%）， 这将影响 normalized\n    v/e 的解读——同样的 absolute v/e 在 Cheetah 中 normalized 更高。 需要 environment-specific calibration，不能直接复用\n    Walker 的 1.5x 阈值。\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_021\n  description: 'Replicate delusional critic in Cheetah Run: dt=2 + subsample ON +\n    trained dt_emb + H=8'\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_return_25K: 160\n    seed0_eval_return_35K: 200\n    seed0_eval_return_45K: 195\n    seed0_eval_return_55K: 180\n    seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 1.35\n    seed0_normalized_ve_45K: 1.45\n    seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 1.5\n    seed0_verdict: DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\n    seed1_eval_return_35K: 220\n    seed1_eval_return_55K: 205\n    seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.25\n    seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 1.38\n    seed1_verdict: DEGRADATION_MILD\n    seed2_eval_return_35K: 185\n    seed2_eval_return_55K: 165\n    seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.4\n    seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 1.52\n    seed2_verdict: DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\n    cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 183\n    cheetah_trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve: 1.35\n    collapse_count: 0\n    vs_baseline_pct_55K: -59%\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：Cheetah Run 中 trained dt_emb 降性能但 collapse 不如 Walker\n    剧烈 （normalized v/e 1.2-1.5x，边界区）。 机制：Cheetah 的 dynamics 比 Walker 更平滑连续，RSSM 在\n    dt=2 的 prediction error 较低。 因此 trained dt_emb 导致的 value overestimation 速度更慢、幅度更小。\n    normalized v/e 在 1.2-1.5x 区间——超过 baseline 但未达到 Walker 的 >2.0x 加速 diverge。 Eval\n    return 呈缓慢下降趋势（200→180）而非 Walker 的急剧 collapse（167→141）。 这产生了关键的 \"environment-dependent\n    modulation\" 叙事： 相同的 dt_embedding 机制在不同 RSSM fidelity 条件下产生不同严重程度。 从方法论看，这其实 *strengthens*\n    而非 weakens 因果解释—— 因为它指向 RSSM prediction quality 作为调节变量，与 C2 机制一致。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cheetah trained dt_emb (3 seeds) vs Walker 008d\n    columns:\n    - env\n    - step\n    - mean_eval\n    - mean_nve\n    - walker_008d_nve\n    - gap\n    rows:\n    - - Cheetah\n      - 25K\n      - 170\n      - 1.2\n      - 1.78\n      - -0.58x\n    - - Cheetah\n      - 35K\n      - 202\n      - 1.33\n      - 1.71\n      - -0.38x\n    - - Cheetah\n      - 45K\n      - 195\n      - 1.42\n      - 2.09\n      - -0.67x\n    - - Cheetah\n      - 55K\n      - 183\n      - 1.47\n      - N/A (collapsed)\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - Cheetah trained dt_emb 3-seed curves vs Cheetah baseline. Degradation visible\n    but no sharp collapse.\n  - 'Cross-environment normalized v/e comparison: Walker 008d (accelerating >2.0x)\n    vs Cheetah (plateau ~1.3-1.5x).'\n  analysis: 'Cheetah 的 trained dt_emb 效果是 \"attenuated Walker\" 而非 \"clean replication\"。\n    这是 median 档的核心挑战：collapse 不复现，但 degradation 和 elevated v/e 复现。 需要 reframe C2：dt_embedding\n    的危害程度由 RSSM fidelity at dt>1 调节。 Walker 的 contact dynamics → 高 RSSM error → 快速\n    collapse。 Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics → 低 RSSM error → 慢速 degradation。 v/e overshoot\n    ratio >1.5x 阈值在 Cheetah 中不是硬界限而是 \"warning zone\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_022\n  description: 'Causal control in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 +\n    H=8'\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_return_35K: 195\n    seed0_eval_return_55K: 220\n    seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 0.82\n    seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 0.75\n    seed1_eval_return_55K: 210\n    seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.8\n    seed2_eval_return_55K: 230\n    seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.72\n    cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 220\n    cross_seed_mean_nve_55K: 0.76\n    cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve: 0.76\n    vs_baseline_pct_55K: -51%\n    vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_eval: +37 (220 vs 183)\n    vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_nve: -0.71x (0.76 vs 1.47)\n  result_rationale: '移除 dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中同样消除 elevated v/e，但 performance gap\n    较 Walker 小。 在 Walker 中，008f vs 008d 的 eval gap 明显（207 vs 141@55K）。 在 Cheetah 中，gap\n    缩小（220 vs 183@55K），因为 baseline degradation 本身较温和。 Normalized v/e 在 0.7-1.15x 范围（median\n    档指标），低于 1.0x 表示 no overestimation。 因果方向仍一致（有 dt_emb → nve>1.2x, 无 dt_emb → nve<1.0x），但\n    effect size 较小。 这支持 \"dt_embedding is harmful but severity is environment-modulated\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cheetah 008f-equivalent vs trained dt_emb (mean across 3 seeds)\n    columns:\n    - config\n    - eval_55K\n    - nve_55K\n    - collapse\n    rows:\n    - - trained dt_emb\n      - 183\n      - 1.47\n      - degradation (no collapse)\n    - - dt_embed_dim=0\n      - 220\n      - 0.76\n      - no degradation\n    - - baseline\n      - 450\n      - 1.0 (reference)\n      - N/A\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Cheetah causal comparison: trained dt_emb (declining, elevated nve) vs dt_embed_dim=0\n    (stable, suppressed nve).'\n  analysis: '因果方向在 Cheetah 仍成立（removing dt_emb → lower v/e + better performance），\n    但 effect size 是 Walker 的约 50%。这是论文中 \"boundary conditions\" section 的核心数据： 当 RSSM\n    prediction quality 较好时（Cheetah），dt_embedding 的危害减轻但不消失。 cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve=0.76\n    落在 median 档指标范围 [0.7, 1.15] 内。\n\n    '\n- name: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_023\n  description: 'Value growth suppression in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample OFF + untrained\n    dt_emb + H=15'\n  expected_results:\n    seed0_eval_return_55K: 380\n    seed0_eval_return_105K: 550\n    seed0_normalized_ve_105K: 0.72\n    seed1_eval_return_105K: 520\n    seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.78\n    seed2_eval_return_105K: 490\n    seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.82\n    cross_seed_mean_105K: 520\n    vs_baseline_pct_105K: -24%\n    v_recovery_count: 1/3 seeds shows V-recovery, 2/3 plateau\n    cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct: 67%\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档假设：Cheetah 中 untrained dt_emb 有保护作用但 gap 较小。 Walker 中\n    008a 达 baseline 85%（778/916），Cheetah 预期只达 67%（520/780）。 原因：Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics\n    使 RSSM error 较低 → trained dt_emb 的危害本就较小 →  untrained dt_emb 的 \"保护效果\" 相对 margin\n    也较小（从 183 到 220 vs 从 141 到 207 in Walker）。 V-recovery pattern 在 Cheetah 中更弱：只有\n    1/3 seeds 出现， 因为 Cheetah 的 reward landscape 更平 → actor 倾向 plateau 而非 oscillate。\n    cheetah_best_dt2_vs_baseline_pct=67% 落在 median 档指标范围 [50%, 75%] 内。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cheetah untrained dt_emb recovery (3 seeds)\n    columns:\n    - step\n    - seed0\n    - seed1\n    - seed2\n    - mean\n    - nve_mean\n    rows:\n    - - 55K\n      - 380\n      - 360\n      - 350\n      - 363\n      - 0.88\n    - - 75K\n      - 420\n      - 440\n      - 410\n      - 423\n      - 0.82\n    - - 105K\n      - 550\n      - 520\n      - 490\n      - 520\n      - 0.77\n  figures_description:\n  - Cheetah 008a-equivalent 3-seed curves. Slow monotonic improvement, fewer oscillations\n    than Walker.\n  - 'Cross-environment untrained dt_emb comparison: Walker shows V-recovery, Cheetah\n    shows plateau-rise.'\n  analysis: 'Cheetah 的 untrained dt_emb configuration 确认 protective effect（no collapse,\n    nve<1.0x） 但 recovery 更缓慢。这与 environment-dependent modulation 假设一致： Cheetah 的 RSSM\n    error 较低 → dt_emb 的影响（有害或保护性的）都被 attenuate。 论文中可用此数据支持 \"the dt_embedding mechanism\n    is general,  but its magnitude scales with RSSM prediction error\"。\n\n    '\n- name: 'RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions'\n  plan_id: plan_030\n  description: Measure observation/reward reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1 from\n    existing trained models across both environments\n  expected_results:\n    walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt1: 4.2\n    walker_rssm_recon_loss_dt2: 6.8\n    walker_dt2_dt1_ratio: 1.62\n    cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt1: 3.9\n    cheetah_rssm_recon_loss_dt2: 5.1\n    cheetah_dt2_dt1_ratio: 1.31\n    walker_reward_pred_error_dt1: 0.08\n    walker_reward_pred_error_dt2: 0.25\n    cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt1: 0.06\n    cheetah_reward_pred_error_dt2: 0.12\n    cross_env_recon_gap_ratio: 1.24\n  result_rationale: '这是 median 档叙事的关键支撑实验——直接量化 RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment dependence。\n    Walker Walk 涉及 contact dynamics（脚与地面碰撞），dt=2 跳过一个接触事件时 RSSM 需要 \"想象\" 中间状态，reconstruction\n    loss 预期升高 ~60%（ratio 1.6x）。 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更平滑（无离散接触切换）， dt=2 的 prediction\n    误差增幅较小（~30%, ratio 1.3x）。 这个 1.6x vs 1.3x 的差距直接解释了为什么 trained dt_emb 在 Walker\n    导致 collapse  而在 Cheetah 仅导致 degradation：更大的 RSSM error → 更多 delusional critic\n    gradient → 更快 collapse。 Reward prediction error 的环境间差异更大（3.1x vs 2.0x ratio），\n    因为 Walker 的 reward 与接触事件强耦合。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'RSSM reconstruction loss: dt=1 vs dt=2 × environment'\n    columns:\n    - environment\n    - loss_dt1\n    - loss_dt2\n    - ratio\n    - reward_err_dt1\n    - reward_err_dt2\n    - reward_ratio\n    rows:\n    - - Walker Walk\n      - 4.2\n      - 6.8\n      - 1.62\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.25\n      - 3.13\n    - - Cheetah Run\n      - 3.9\n      - 5.1\n      - 1.31\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.12\n      - 2.0\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: RSSM reconstruction loss at dt=1 vs dt=2 for both environments. Walker\n    gap visibly larger.'\n  - 'Scatter: RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio (x) vs peak normalized v/e in trained dt_emb config\n    (y). Two points but on the expected trend line.'\n  analysis: 'plan_030 提供了 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 假设的 mechanistic foundation。\n    Walker 的 RSSM dt2/dt1 gap 比 Cheetah 大 ~24%（1.62/1.31=1.24x）， 这与 Walker 中 trained\n    dt_emb 导致更严重 collapse 的观察一致。 但只有两个环境点，无法建立 quantitative 关系。 论文中应呈现为 \"consistent\n    with the hypothesis\" 而非 \"proves\"。 如果 plan_040（Hopper Hop）执行，将提供第三个点。\n\n    '\n- name: Actor entropy analysis\n  plan_id: plan_031\n  description: Plot actor entropy vs training step for healthy (008a/008c/008f) vs\n    collapsed (006/008d) configurations\n  expected_results:\n    walker_008d_entropy_25K: 3.8\n    walker_008d_entropy_35K: 4.1\n    walker_008d_entropy_45K: 4.5\n    walker_008d_entropy_trend: increasing\n    walker_006_entropy_35K: 3.9\n    walker_006_entropy_55K: 5.2\n    walker_006_entropy_trend: sharply_increasing\n    walker_008a_entropy_55K: 3.2\n    walker_008a_entropy_105K: 2.8\n    walker_008a_entropy_trend: stable_to_decreasing\n    walker_008f_entropy_35K: 3.5\n    walker_008f_entropy_trend: stable\n    walker_baseline_entropy_35K: 3.0\n    walker_baseline_entropy_105K: 2.5\n    walker_baseline_entropy_trend: decreasing\n  result_rationale: 'Actor entropy 增高表示 policy 变得更随机——这是 delusional critic gradient\n    的下游症状。 当 value function 高估 → actor 收到 misleading gradient → policy 不再有 clear preference\n    → entropy 升高。 预期 collapsed configs（008d, 006）显示 entropy 单调上升（actor confusion），\n    而 healthy configs（008a, 008f, baseline）显示 entropy stable 或下降（policy sharpening）。\n    这不是新发现，但提供了 mechanism 的额外 sanity check： 如果 collapsed configs 的 entropy *不*上升，则\n    C2 的 \"delusional critic → actor degradation\" 链需要修正。 Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 noise\n    较大（因为 entropy 是 high-variance metric）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Actor entropy trajectories\n    columns:\n    - config\n    - entropy_25K\n    - entropy_35K\n    - entropy_45K\n    - entropy_55K\n    - trend\n    rows:\n    - - baseline\n      - 3.2\n      - 3.0\n      - 2.9\n      - 2.8\n      - decreasing\n    - - 008d (collapse)\n      - 3.8\n      - 4.1\n      - 4.5\n      - —\n      - increasing\n    - - 006 (collapse)\n      - 3.5\n      - 3.9\n      - 4.2\n      - 5.2\n      - sharply increasing\n    - - 008a (V-recovery)\n      - 3.3\n      - 3.1\n      - 3.0\n      - 3.2\n      - stable\n    - - 008f (stable)\n      - 3.4\n      - 3.5\n      - 3.3\n      - —\n      - stable\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Actor entropy over training: collapsed configs diverge upward, healthy configs\n    converge downward. Clear separation after 25K.'\n  analysis: 'Entropy analysis 为 C2 提供 corroborating evidence 而非 primary evidence。\n    Collapsed configs 的 entropy 上升模式与 \"delusional critic → actor confusion\" 一致。 在\n    paper 中作为 supplementary figure 或 appendix，支撑 main text 的 causal diagram。\n\n    '\n- name: Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\n  plan_id: plan_032\n  description: Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return for trained vs untrained\n    dt_emb\n  expected_results:\n    walker_008d_value_mc_correlation: 0.35\n    walker_008d_value_bias: +45% (systematic overestimation)\n    walker_008d_value_std_ratio: 2.1\n    walker_008a_value_mc_correlation: 0.72\n    walker_008a_value_bias: +8% (mild overestimation)\n    walker_008a_value_std_ratio: 1.2\n    walker_baseline_value_mc_correlation: 0.85\n    walker_baseline_value_bias: +5%\n    walker_baseline_value_std_ratio: 1.1\n    walker_008f_value_mc_correlation: 0.68\n    walker_008f_value_bias: +10%\n    walker_008f_value_std_ratio: 1.3\n  result_rationale: 'V(s) vs MC return 的联合分布揭示 v/e ratio 无法捕捉的细节。 008d（trained dt_emb,\n    collapse）预期显示：(a) systematic positive bias（值线远高于 y=x）， (b) 低相关性（value 与实际 return\n    decouple），(c) 高 variance ratio（value 在不确定状态大幅波动）。 这三个特征共同构成 \"delusional critic\"\n    的 distributional fingerprint。 008a/008f（healthy configs）预期接近 baseline 分布，bias\n    小、相关性高。 Median 档下预期 pattern 清晰但 008f 的 correlation 略低于 baseline （因为 dt=2 imagination\n    本身引入了一些 noise，即使没有 dt_embedding）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Value calibration summary\n    columns:\n    - config\n    - correlation\n    - bias_pct\n    - variance_ratio\n    - verdict\n    rows:\n    - - baseline\n      - 0.85\n      - +5%\n      - 1.1\n      - calibrated\n    - - 008a (untrained)\n      - 0.72\n      - +8%\n      - 1.2\n      - mildly_optimistic\n    - - 008f (no dt_emb)\n      - 0.68\n      - +10%\n      - 1.3\n      - mildly_optimistic\n    - - 008d (trained)\n      - 0.35\n      - +45%\n      - 2.1\n      - delusional\n  figures_description:\n  - '2×2 scatter plot grid: V(s) vs MC return for baseline, 008a, 008f, 008d. Each\n    with y=x line and regression fit.'\n  - 'Histogram: value prediction error distribution (V(s) - MC) for each config. 008d\n    shows heavy right tail.'\n  analysis: 'Distribution analysis 将 v/e ratio proxy 升级为更 rigorous 的 value calibration\n    证据。 008d 的 correlation=0.35 和 bias=+45% 直接证明 \"delusional\"——value function 的预测\n    与实际 return 几乎 decouple 且系统性偏高。 这是 paper 中最强的 supplementary evidence，值得在 main text\n    中给一段或一个 figure。\n\n    '\n- name: dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\n  plan_id: plan_033\n  description: 'Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors: cosine similarity between dt=1\n    and dt=2'\n  expected_results:\n    cosine_sim_5K: 0.92\n    cosine_sim_15K: 0.75\n    cosine_sim_35K: 0.42\n    cosine_sim_55K: 0.28\n    embedding_norm_dt1_35K: 1.2\n    embedding_norm_dt2_35K: 2.8\n    embedding_divergence_onset: ~15K-25K (coincides with v/e acceleration)\n  result_rationale: 'Trained dt_embedding 在训练过程中逐步学会区分 dt=1 和 dt=2。 早期（<10K）dt=1 和\n    dt=2 embedding 相似（cosine~0.9），value function 尚未 exploit 差异。 15-25K 时 embedding\n    开始分离（cosine 下降到 0.5-0.7）， 这恰好与 v/e ratio 开始加速的时间窗口吻合。 这提供了 temporal evidence：dt_embedding\n    的学习 → value function 开始 exploit → overestimation → collapse。 dt=2 embedding 的\n    norm 增大（2.8 vs dt=1 的 1.2）表明 value function 放大了 dt=2 的表征， 可能因为 dt=2 transition\n    在 imagination 中产生更大的 \"value opportunity\"（但实际是虚假的）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: dt_embedding evolution during training\n    columns:\n    - step\n    - cosine_sim\n    - norm_dt1\n    - norm_dt2\n    - nve_at_step\n    rows:\n    - - 5K\n      - 0.92\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.9\n      - ~1.0x\n    - - 15K\n      - 0.75\n      - 1.0\n      - 1.4\n      - ~1.2x\n    - - 25K\n      - 0.55\n      - 1.1\n      - 2.1\n      - ~1.5x\n    - - 35K\n      - 0.42\n      - 1.2\n      - 2.8\n      - ~1.7x\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dual-axis plot: cosine similarity (decreasing) and normalized v/e (increasing)\n    vs training step. Divergence onset co-occurs.'\n  - 2D PCA of dt_embedding at [5K, 15K, 25K, 35K]. dt=1 and dt=2 clusters separate\n    over training.\n  analysis: 'Cosine similarity 分析提供 mechanistic timeline：embedding 分离 → value exploitation\n    → collapse。 这是 P2 priority 因为它补充而非替代 core evidence， 但在论文中可以做一个很有说服力的 timeline\n    figure。 如果 embedding 的分离时间与 v/e 加速不吻合，则 C2 的 mechanism story 需要修正。\n\n    '\n- name: Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\n  plan_id: plan_040\n  description: 'Third DMC environment: baseline + trained dt_emb + dt_embed_dim=0'\n  expected_results:\n    baseline_asymptotic: 250\n    trained_dtEmb_peak: 120\n    trained_dtEmb_nve_peak: 1.55\n    trained_dtEmb_collapse: partial (1/3 seeds collapse, 2/3 degradation)\n    no_dtEmb_eval_55K: 105\n    no_dtEmb_nve_55K: 0.85\n    baseline_ve_stable: 55-62%\n  result_rationale: 'Hopper Hop 是高难度 DMC task（baseline ~250 远低于 Walker ~950 和 Cheetah\n    ~780）。 RSSM prediction quality 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间 （有 hopping contact events\n    但比 walking 更规律）。 Median 档下预期 trained dt_emb 的 normalized v/e 在 Walker 和 Cheetah\n    之间（~1.5x）， 1/3 seeds collapse，2/3 degradation。 dt_embed_dim=0 仍应 stable（nve <1.0x）。\n    但 Hopper 的 absolute performance 很低，signal-to-noise ratio 差 →  结论 less conclusive，主要价值是提供\n    plan_030 scatter plot 的第三个点。 P2 priority，论文如时间不够可省略。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Hopper Hop results summary\n    columns:\n    - config\n    - mean_eval_55K\n    - mean_nve_55K\n    - collapse_fraction\n    rows:\n    - - baseline\n      - 180\n      - 1.0 (ref)\n      - 0/3\n    - - trained dt_emb\n      - 95\n      - 1.55\n      - 1/3\n    - - dt_embed_dim=0\n      - 105\n      - 0.85\n      - 0/3\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Three-environment summary: RSSM dt2/dt1 ratio vs peak normalized v/e. Three points\n    showing positive trend.'\n  analysis: Hopper 作为第三环境，主要贡献是验证 environment-dependent modulation 假设。 如果 RSSM dt2/dt1\n    ratio 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（如 plan_030 预测）， 且 normalized v/e 也介于两者之间，则三个点落在一条正相关趋势线上——\n    这将 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 从 post-hoc 假设升级为 empirical pattern。 但 P2\n    priority 意味着在 CoRL deadline 前可能无法完成。 Median 档论文即使没有 Hopper 也可以成立，用 Discussion\n    中的 \"boundary conditions\" 段覆盖。\n","numLines":884,"startLine":1,"totalLines":884}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013YUeZGzdjg3iB9KsXtrXfo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full PDF (9 pages) and the review context YAML. Let me now dispatch two reviewer agents in parallel:\n\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nThen I'll conduct the full roundtable process. Let me launch both reviewers simultaneously.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26466,"cache_read_input_tokens":22971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26466},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a90c8859-8e50-4bd7-a75e-c4f31c8dbc1b","uuid":"8adb1932-23e4-41bb-b6a3-ff90ab2a8c49"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013YUeZGzdjg3iB9KsXtrXfo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PDF 和实验设计参考已读取完毕。现在启动两位 Reviewer 进行独立审稿。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26466,"cache_read_input_tokens":22971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26466},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a90c8859-8e50-4bd7-a75e-c4f31c8dbc1b","uuid":"a8b83f2b-634c-4faa-9cf2-c79ab28d59e8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013YUeZGzdjg3iB9KsXtrXfo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014d7hPc915VYYwTzJNDc6So","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a top ML venue review. Your focus areas are **methodology** and **experiments**. Review the paper below thoroughly and produce a structured review.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** \"Diagnosing Value Overestimation in Temporally-Abstract World Models\"\n\nThe paper investigates why variable-rate imagination (Δt>1) degrades performance in DreamerV3. Through factorial experiments across 3 DMC environments (Walker Walk, Cheetah Run, Hopper Hop), 3 seeds each, and controlled ablations of temporal embedding, the paper establishes a causal chain: trained Δt-embedding enables the value function to exploit imprecise RSSM predictions at Δt>1, producing systematic value overestimation (\"delusional critic\") that drives policy collapse. Removing or freezing the embedding eliminates the pathology. Severity scales with RSSM prediction-quality gap between environments.\n\n**Key configurations tested:**\n- Baseline: Δt=1, standard DreamerV3\n- 008d: Subsample ON + trained Δt-emb + H=8 (collapse condition)\n- 008f: Subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8 (causal control)\n- 008a: Subsample OFF + untrained Δt-emb + H=15 (value suppression)\n\n**Core findings:**\n1. Trained Δt-embedding is the primary contributing factor to value overestimation collapse in Walker Walk (2/3 seeds collapse, 1/3 degradation; nve>1.5× in all seeds)\n2. Removing Δt-embedding (dt_embed_dim=0) eliminates collapse across all seeds and environments\n3. Environment-dependent modulation: Walker Walk (high RSSM gap, 1.62×) collapses; Cheetah Run (low gap, 1.31×) degrades gradually; Hopper Hop falls in between\n4. Untrained (frozen-random) Δt-embedding suppresses value growth, prevents collapse, 2/3 seeds show V-shaped recovery in Walker Walk\n5. Normalised v/e overshoot ratio proposed as diagnostic heuristic (≥1.5× threshold, environment-dependent)\n\n**Methodology (Section 3):**\n- Base: DreamerV3 with default hyperparameters on DMC\n- Variable-rate imagination: Δt-embedding e(Δt) ∈ R^d concatenated to RSSM input\n- Three embedding regimes: trained, untrained (frozen-random), removed (d=0)\n- Factorial design: 3 factors (embedding type, temporal subsampling ON/OFF, imagination horizon H=8/H=15)\n- Diagnostic metric: normalised v/e overshoot ratio = v/e_experiment(t) / v/e_baseline(t)\n\n**Experiments (Section 4):**\n- 4.1: Walker Walk baseline calibration (3 seeds, CV<2%, v/e stable at 67-74%)\n- 4.2: 008d collapse replication (2/3 seeds collapse, all nve>1.5×)\n- 4.3: 008f stability (all nve converges to 0.68-0.82×, no collapse)\n- 4.4: 008a V-recovery (nve<1.0× all seeds, V-recovery in 2/3, mean 693 at 105K)\n- 4.5: Cheetah Run environment-dependent modulation (degradation not collapse, nve 1.47× vs Walker's >2.0×)\n- 4.6: RSSM prediction quality analysis (Walker dt2/dt1 ratio 1.62 vs Cheetah 1.31)\n- 4.7: Hopper Hop third-environment validation (nve 1.55×, 1/3 collapse)\n- 4.8: Actor entropy analysis (collapsed configs show increasing entropy, healthy configs stable/decreasing)\n- 4.9: Value calibration V(s) vs MC return (008d: correlation 0.35, bias +45%, variance ratio 2.1)\n- 4.10: Δt-embedding divergence timeline (cosine similarity drops from 0.92 to 0.42, co-occurs with nve acceleration)\n\n**Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml):**\nThe full experiment design includes these imagined experiments:\n1. Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2 (plan_010) — COVERED in paper Table 1\n2. Walker Walk 008d seeds 1-2 (plan_011) — COVERED in paper Table 2\n3. Walker Walk 008f seeds 1-2 (plan_012) — COVERED in paper Table 3\n4. Walker Walk 008a seeds 1-2 (plan_013) — COVERED in paper Table 4\n5. Cheetah Run baseline 3 seeds (plan_020) — COVERED in paper Table 5\n6. Cheetah Run trained dt_emb 3 seeds (plan_021) — COVERED in paper Tables 6-7\n7. Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 3 seeds (plan_022) — COVERED in paper Table 7\n8. Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb 3 seeds (plan_023) — COVERED in paper Table 8\n9. RSSM prediction quality dt=1 vs dt=2 (plan_030) — COVERED in paper Table 9\n10. Actor entropy analysis (plan_031) — COVERED in paper Table 11\n11. Value prediction distribution vs MC returns (plan_032) — COVERED in paper Table 12\n12. dt_embedding cosine similarity (plan_033) — COVERED in paper Table 13\n13. Hopper Hop validation 3 seeds × 3 configs (plan_040) — COVERED in paper Table 10\n\n## Review Instructions\n\nEvaluate the paper on these dimensions, rating each 1-10:\n\n1. **Methodological soundness**: Is the factorial experiment design appropriate? Are the ablations well-controlled? Is the causal reasoning valid? Are there confounds?\n2. **Experimental rigor**: Are results statistically reliable? Are there enough seeds? Is the evaluation thorough? Are comparisons fair?\n3. **Clarity of experimental presentation**: Are tables/figures well-organized? Is it easy to follow the experimental logic?\n4. **Completeness of experiments**: Are there missing experiments that would strengthen the claims? How well does the paper cover the planned experiment set?\n5. **Soundness of the diagnostic metric (nve)**: Is the normalised v/e ratio well-motivated? Are its limitations adequately discussed?\n\nFor each dimension, provide:\n- Rating (1-10)\n- Key strengths\n- Key weaknesses\n- Specific suggestions\n\nThen provide:\n- **Overall assessment** of methodology and experiments\n- **Top 3 strengths**\n- **Top 3 weaknesses**\n- **Questions for authors**\n- **Overall score** (1-6 scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept)\n- **Confidence** (1-5: 1=low, 5=expert)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. This is a diagnostic/analysis paper, not an algorithm paper — judge it on the quality of its scientific investigation.","model":"opus","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":26466,"cache_read_input_tokens":22971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":26466},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a90c8859-8e50-4bd7-a75e-c4f31c8dbc1b","uuid":"3dfadcd2-f86c-4ff4-8925-fda71c43c12b"}
